# Database (PostgreSQL + Prisma)

## Integrity

- Enforce uniqueness, FKs, NOT NULL in the database — not only in app code.
- Use transactions when multiple writes must succeed/fail together (e.g. accept bid + payment event).
- Do not use transactions for simple reads.

## Naming

- DB identifiers: `snake_case` (`created_at`, `user_profiles`).
- TypeScript: `camelCase` via Prisma mapping.

## Migrations

- Every schema change = versioned Prisma migration.
- No manual prod DDL. No destructive data loss without explicit approval.

## Performance

- Index for real query patterns; avoid indexing everything.
- Prevent N+1; paginate large lists (`page`/`limit`).
- Select only needed fields when payloads are large.

## Money / IDs (Clox)

- Money as integer **cents AUD**.
- Prefer UUIDs for public IDs (split-ready).
